<header><p class="st-kicker">other · British Isles</p><h1 class="st-title">Northern Ireland</h1><p class="st-meta">1921 CE – present · capital Belfast</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The part of the United Kingdom in north-east Ireland, created by partition in 1921 and marked by decades of conflict and a power-sharing peace.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/government-of-ireland-act-1920">Government of Ireland Act 1920</a> created Northern Ireland from six of Ulster's nine counties, where Protestants, mostly unionists, were a majority. Its Parliament opened in June 1921, and it opted out of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/irish-free-state">Irish Free State</a> in December 1922.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Northern Ireland was governed for fifty years by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ulster-unionist-party">Ulster Unionist Party</a> from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stormont">Stormont</a>, with discrimination against the Catholic, mainly nationalist minority. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belfast">Belfast</a> was a centre of shipbuilding and linen. The civil rights movement of the late 1960s was followed by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/the-troubles">Troubles</a>, which killed about 3,600 people, and direct rule from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a> from 1972.</p><h2>To the present</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/good-friday-agreement">Good Friday Agreement</a> of 1998 established a power-sharing Assembly and Executive and confirmed that Northern Ireland remains in the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-kingdom">United Kingdom</a> unless its people vote otherwise.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/northern-ireland.jpg" alt="Northern Ireland" width="320" height="270"><figcaption>Image: maix; derivative work by Alphathon /'æɫfə.θɒn · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Northern_Ireland_in_the_UK_and_Europe.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1921 CE – present</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/21st-century">21st century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>other</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Belfast</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>James Craig, Terence O'Neill, Ian Paisley</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Christianity; Protestant and Catholic</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>English, Irish, Ulster Scots</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/united-kingdom">United Kingdom</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Ulster</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1974&amp;focus=northern-ireland" aria-label="Northern Ireland on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4549 308 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Northern Ireland lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M4869 564L4997 651M4869 564L4997 651"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M4997 651h0M4997 651h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4869 564h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M4869 564h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Belfast. <a href="/atlas?year=1974&amp;focus=northern-ireland">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

